# Production env key list. Prefer generating it: `make prod-env` (asks only the
# app URL, generates every secret from deploy/env/schema) and
# `make prod-env-upgrade` for new releases; see docs/DEVELOPMENT.md. Manual
# route: copy .env.example to `.env.server`, replace every secret, then add the
# production-only keys below. Usage: make prod-config / make prod-up
#
# Required besides .env.example values (compose.prod.yml fails without them):
#   NAME_PREFIX (unique per app on a host; names containers, volumes and the app
#   network; the schema default is `rentopia`) / APP_NETWORK_NAME,
#   BACKEND_IMAGE, FRONTEND_IMAGE, SITE_IMAGE,
#   DB_USER, DB_NAME, DB_PASSWORD, REDIS_PASSWORD, MEILI_MASTER_KEY,
#   S3_BUCKET, S3_ACCESS_KEY, S3_SECRET_KEY,
#   JWT_ACCESS_SECRET, JWT_REFRESH_SECRET, AUTH_SECRET, AUTH_URL, AUTH_ADAPTER_SECRET,
#   APP_ENCRYPTION_KEY (never change after the first deploy: it seals integration
#   credentials, OAuth secrets and personal data),
#   SITE_EMBED_SECRET (site + frontend widget signatures, >= 32 chars),
#   CENTRIFUGO_API_KEY, CENTRIFUGO_TOKEN_HMAC_SECRET, CENTRIFUGO_WS_URL,
#   CENTRIFUGO_ALLOWED_ORIGINS, CORS_ALLOWED_ORIGINS,
#   WUZAPI_ADMIN_TOKEN, WUZAPI_ENCRYPTION_KEY (wuzapi WhatsApp gateway).
#
# Production-only keys (not in .env.example):
#   APP_URL          the public app URL; the schema derives AUTH_URL,
#                    PUBLIC_FRONTEND_URL, CORS / Centrifugo origins, SITE_BASE_URL from it
#   REALTIME_HOST    Centrifugo domain (default realtime.<app host>)
#   WUZAPI_IMAGE     wuzapi image; pin a tested tag (default asternic/wuzapi:latest)
#   WUZAPI_ENCRYPTION_KEY  wuzapi's own at-rest key
# compose.prod.yml sets the internal hosts itself (DB_HOST, REDIS_ADDR, S3_ENDPOINT,
# MEILI_HOST, CENTRIFUGO_API_URL, WUZAPI_BASE_URL, WUZAPI_WEBHOOK_BASE_URL, API_URL)
# as <service>.${APP_NETWORK_NAME}; do not set them here.
#
# Product: TENANCY_ENABLED=true (schema default; organizations are the product),
#   TENANCY_SELF_SERVE (default false), TENANCY_CACHE_TTL (default 60s).
#
# Mail (fill in to send e-mail): SMTP_HOST, SMTP_PORT, SMTP_USERNAME,
#   SMTP_PASSWORD, MAIL_FROM, MAIL_FROM_NAME.
#
# Provider endpoints (credentials are per organization, set in the panel):
#   IYZICO_SANDBOX_BASE_URL, IYZICO_LIVE_BASE_URL, NETGSM_LIVE_BASE_URL,
#   NETGSM_SANDBOX_BASE_URL (leave empty: Netgsm has no sandbox),
#   SMS_LOG_PROVIDER (ignored in production). E-invoice, KABİS, HGS, Yolcu360
#   and Obilet have no env keys; fake providers are never registered in production.
#
# Branded site custom domains (optional): SITE_DOMAIN_TARGET_HOST,
#   SITE_DOMAIN_TARGET_IPS, SITE_DOMAIN_PROVISIONER (manual | traefik_file |
#   dokploy), SITE_DOMAIN_TRAEFIK_DIR, DOKPLOY_URL, DOKPLOY_API_KEY,
#   DOKPLOY_COMPOSE_ID, DOKPLOY_SITE_SERVICE, DOKPLOY_SITE_PORT.
#
# Environment: APP_ENV (schema default production; set staging on a staging
#   stack). Backend, worker, frontend and site read it; it is the error
#   tracking environment. Outside production the official KABİS, e-invoice and
#   Netgsm endpoints are refused unless KABIS_ALLOW_PRODUCTION_IN_NON_PROD /
#   EINVOICE_ALLOW_PRODUCTION_IN_NON_PROD / NETGSM_ALLOW_PRODUCTION_IN_NON_PROD
#   is true (default false; ignored in production). See
#   docs/operations/observability.md.
#
# Optional error tracking (Sentry protocol): BACKEND_SENTRY_DSN (backend +
#   worker), FRONTEND_SENTRY_DSN (frontend), SITE_SENTRY_DSN (site),
#   SENTRY_ENVIRONMENT (all, default APP_ENV), SENTRY_RELEASE (all, optional),
#   SENTRY_TRACES_SAMPLE_RATE (backend, default 0). Empty = off.
#
# Optional failed-work alerts: ALERT_EMAIL (e-mail copy of the in-app alerts to
#   platform admins; one per job kind per 15 minutes). Empty = in-app only.
#
# Optional Web Push / mobile: VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY, VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY, VAPID_SUBJECT
#   (generated by the schema), EXPO_ACCESS_TOKEN.
#
# Optional mobile auth (backend + worker, see .env.example): AUTH_REVIEW_ACCOUNTS,
#   AUTH_APPLE_NATIVE_CLIENT_IDS, AUTH_GOOGLE_NATIVE_CLIENT_IDS,
#   AUTH_QR_TRUST_GEO_HEADERS, AUTH_QR_GEOIP_DB, and the Sign in with Apple key
#   fallback AUTH_APPLE_TEAM_ID / AUTH_APPLE_KEY_ID / AUTH_APPLE_PRIVATE_KEY
#   (not needed when the .p8 is uploaded in Platform → Integrations → Apple).
#
# Backups (optional; scripts/backup.sh, docs/operations/backup-restore.md):
#   COMPOSE_PROFILES           `backup` starts the scheduled backup service (default empty = off)
#   BACKUP_AGE_RECIPIENT       age public key(s), comma separated (default empty; backups refuse
#                              to run without it; the private key stays off the server)
#   BACKUP_DIR                 host directory of the encrypted sets (default /var/backups/<NAME_PREFIX>)
#   BACKUP_TIME                daily run time, HH:MM Europe/Istanbul (default 03:15)
#   BACKUP_KEEP_DAILY          newest set of each of the last N days (default 7)
#   BACKUP_KEEP_WEEKLY         newest set of each of the last N weeks (default 4)
#   BACKUP_OFFSITE_ENDPOINT    off-site S3 endpoint (default empty)
#   BACKUP_OFFSITE_REGION      off-site region (default empty = us-east-1)
#   BACKUP_OFFSITE_BUCKET      off-site bucket; set = upload every set (default empty = off)
#   BACKUP_OFFSITE_ACCESS_KEY  off-site write-only key (default empty)
#   BACKUP_OFFSITE_SECRET_KEY  off-site secret (default empty)
#
# Plain Docker host only (Dokploy creates it): docker network create dokploy-network
#
# See .env.example for every key with its comment. Start from:
#   make prod-env            (preferred)
#   cp .env.example .env.server
